  "note": "Fort emplacement collar, intact state: the pieces a tight concrete parapet ring is built from (four swapped edge pieces and four inner corners), all cut from ONE contiguous 5x5 plate painted in a single ImageGen pass from templates/fort-emplacement-guide.png (fort-emplacement-guide.py) with the fort's own concrete as material reference (templates/fort-material-reference.png); exact prompt retained (fort-emplacement.prompt.txt), raw retained unmodified. ImageGen painted the plate 868x840 rather than 960x960, so the rects are measured and authoritative. Doodads, not a block: the collar is stamped swapped (the north ring cell wears the south-edge piece) and no GridLayout resolves that. The ids are the CoverPropDamage family, so rounds wear each piece intact -> damaged -> destroyed. Presentation art only - cover and topology belong to the post or pad that stamps it.",
